---
// Blog post. Copy authored against briefs/male-vs-female-maltipoo.json (2026-07-13).
// Evidence: standard chooser topic; names female 10/mo
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PawTrail from '../../components/PawTrail.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import FactsCard from '../../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../../assets/site/40-maltipoo-pair-bandanas.webp';

const title = 'Male or Female Maltipoo? The Small Differences | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Male vs female Maltipoo: the real behavioural differences (smaller than folklore says), marking and season practicalities, sterilisation timing.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Blog', url: '/blog' },
  { name: 'Male vs Female', url: '/blog/male-vs-female-maltipoo' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "Are male Maltipoos more affectionate?",
    a: "On average, faintly; in practice, the individual puppy decides. Our placement notes on each puppy beat the folklore.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do female Maltipoos cost more?",
    a: "Market-wide, females often list slightly higher; within our range the drivers stay colour and size, not sex.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is marking guaranteed in males?",
    a: "No; early sterilisation and clean toilet training prevent it in most. An intact adolescent male may experiment, and the phase manages out.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which is easier for first-time owners?",
    a: "Genuinely neither. First-timers do best choosing the calm-confident puppy of either sex, which is exactly what we point out at viewings.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I get a male or female Maltipoo?",
    a: "Choose the individual puppy, not the chromosome: the personality overlap dwarfs the average sex difference. Meet the litter, watch which puppy chooses you, and let sex be the tiebreaker at most.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do female Maltipoos come into season?",
    a: "Intact females come into season roughly twice a year, with spotting and suitor attention for a few weeks, until sterilised from around seven months. In an HDB flat it is managed with routine and hygiene rather than drama.",
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/blog/male-vs-female-maltipoo',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Male vs female Maltipoo differences',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/blog/male-vs-female-maltipoo" schemas={schemas}>
  <article>
    <section class="container-site pt-4">
      <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12 relative overflow-hidden rise-in">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="absolute -top-8 -right-8 w-44 h-44 text-white/40" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute top-6 right-[22%] w-9 h-9 text-primary/25 float-soft" style="--float-rot: 14deg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute bottom-5 right-[10%] w-7 h-7 text-primary/20 float-soft" style="--float-rot: -10deg; animation-delay: -2.6s" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute -bottom-10 -left-10 w-40 h-40 text-primary/8" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <div class="absolute bottom-2 left-0 right-0 opacity-30"><PawTrail /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="relative">
        <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Choosing</p>
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[26ch]">Male or female Maltipoo?</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft m-0">By {site.owners}, AVS licensed pet shop owners · Updated 13 July 2026</p>
      </div></div>
    </section>

    <AnswerCapsule question='Should you choose a male or female Maltipoo?'>
      Choose the individual puppy, not the chromosome: within this breed the personality overlap dwarfs the average difference. The practical distinctions are pre-sterilisation ones (marking in males, seasons in females), and both fade after sterilisation from around seven months. Meet the litter; pick the temperament.
    </AnswerCapsule>

    <section class="container-site py-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1.6fr_1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="pop p-6 md:p-8 text-ink-soft space-y-5 max-w-[72ch]">
          <img data-tilt src={featuredImg.src} width={featuredImg.width} height={featuredImg.height} alt="Two apricot Maltipoos of different shades sitting side by side wearing olive and terracotta bandanas" loading="lazy" class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]" />
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">The folklore versus the overlap</h2>
          <p>
            The folk wisdom says males are clingier and goofier, females more independent and quicker to mature, and across thousands of dogs the averages lean faintly that way. But in a breed where every individual is bred for devotion, the overlap swallows the difference: the cuddliest dog we have placed this year was a female, the most dignified a male.
          </p>
          <p>
            Meeting the actual litter beats the theory every time. Watch which puppy chooses you, ask us about each one's observed character, and let sex be the tiebreaker at most.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">The practical pre-sterilisation differences</h2>
          <p>
            Intact males may start leg-lift marking as adolescence arrives; intact females come into season roughly twice a year, with spotting and unwanted suitor attention for a few weeks. In an HDB flat, both are managed with routine and hygiene rather than drama, and both are temporary decisions rather than lifetime features.
          </p>
          <p>
            Sterilisation from around <a href="/maltipoo-lifespan-health">seven months</a>, per your vet’s timing, retires most of it, and drops the AVS licence to $13.50 a year or the one-time $35 lifetime rate, as the <a href="/maltipoo-price-singapore">price guide</a> notes.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Choosing in practice</h2>
          <p>
            Households with a resident dog often find <a href="/blog/maltipoo-second-dog">opposite-sex introductions</a> smoothest, which is the one scenario where sex genuinely earns a vote. Otherwise, rank your real preferences: temperament first, colour and size second, sex a distant third.
          </p>
          <p>
            A note from the shop floor: buyers who arrive fixed on one sex and meet the litter usually leave with whichever puppy climbed into their lap first. We consider that the correct outcome.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Does sex change size, coat or price?</h2>
          <p>
            Marginally, occasionally, and no. Males in a litter often finish a few hundred grams heavier, but within a 2 to 4kg toy breed the overlap swallows the difference; we have placed 2.2kg males and 3.8kg females without the world ending. Coat texture and colour follow the parents, not the sex, so an apricot female and her apricot brother grey out or deepen on the same schedule.
          </p>
          <p>
            Price at our counter is set by expected adult size and colour within the $3,288 to $5,988 all-in range, never by sex. A shop quoting a premium "because female" is telling you about its marketing, not its dogs.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">The behaviour myths, retired one by one</h2>
          <p>
            "Males mark indoors forever": intact males may experiment during adolescence; sterilised-early males in flats mostly never start, and the fix is the same <a href="/blog/maltipoo-potty-training">toilet system</a> either way. "Females are moodier": a female's twice-yearly season before sterilisation brings two clingy, nappy-wearing weeks, after it, temperament tracks the individual. "Males are more affectionate": in this breed everyone is; affection is the breed feature, not a sex feature.
          </p>
          <p>
            The honest summary from a hundred-plus placements: the spread within each sex dwarfs the gap between them. Meet the litter, watch for the temperament you want, and let the folklore stay in the group chat.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:sticky md:top-24">
        <FactsCard
          heading='Male vs female card'
          items={[
            "Personality: overlap dwarfs the averages",
            "Males intact: possible marking phase",
            "Females intact: ~2 seasons a year",
            "Sterilisation retires both + cuts licence fee",
            "Pick temperament; let sex tiebreak"
          ]}
        />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FAQ items={faqItems} />

    <CtaClose
      secondaryHeading='Meet the litter'
      secondaryText='Temperaments on display beat theory: come see who chooses you.'
      secondaryHref='/puppies'
      secondaryLabel='See available puppies'
    />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
